/-!
# Construction of the characteristic-two component: proved reductions

The internal module and faithful FF action use the genuine generalized
Fitting equality, source Sylow conclusion, and nontrivial Thompson image.
Characteristic two descends to intermediate Sylow overgroups, permitting
minimization in the actual outside family. The commutator argument uses the
source action-kernel and normalizer identities and the C-component orbit
bound. Its three-prime core centralizes the component modulo the two-core.
Classified star candidates already imply the solvable-invariant subgroup
containment, with solvability of `Y₊S` proved from its three-group quotient.
The complete A.3.6 alternatives upgrade a candidate's two-core quotient
to a quasisimple group and supply the exact `ComponentWitness`.

The source results 15.3.15(2) and 15.3.26(2) are not yet assembled here.
The remaining steps are selection of `StarComponentCandidate` and its orbit
bound from the actual B.5.6 alternatives, and instantiation of the universal
A.3.6 source theorem. Neither existence nor that classification theorem is
included in the standing local data. The conditional solvable-control
results must also be instantiated for every smaller outside overgroup.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
printed pp.1123–1126 and 1130.
-/
